cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "pypdb2pov: PDB and mmCIF Structures as POV-Ray Scenes"
abstract: >
  pypdb2pov converts PDB and PDBx/mmCIF atomic structures into POV-Ray
  scenes for ray-traced molecular graphics. It is a Python port of the
  1993 C program pdb2pov by the same author, keeping its command-line
  vocabulary while reading modern mmCIF, resolving elements from the
  columns the format actually defines, and finding bonds with a spatial
  grid rather than an all-pairs scan. The package has no runtime
  dependencies and bundles the POV-Ray include files that give each
  element its own texture.
